Real-Life BSE Example
Suppose every night BSE receives:
trade_day1.csv
trade_day2.csv
trade_day3.csv
Single Processing
Read Day1
↓
Validate Day1
↓
Transform Day1
↓
Load Day1

Then Day2

Then Day3
If each file takes 10 minutes:
10 + 10 + 10 = 30 minutes
Multiprocessing
Three worker processes run simultaneously:
Worker 1 → Day1
Worker 2 → Day2
Worker 3 → Day3
All finish in approximately:
≈10 minutes
________________________________________
Key Interview Point
•	Single Processing: One CPU core executes one task at a time. Simpler but slower for independent tasks. 
•	Multiprocessing: Multiple CPU cores execute independent tasks in parallel. Faster for CPU-intensive or independent workloads like processing many files simultaneously.


